\fs28 \cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 Jenitta Gnana 0 minutes 3 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 But we have many kind of projects within Australia, but I thought what we could do creatively is do a project for RMIT's research and development department. So R&D is typically a black box from, you know, university's key enterprise and IT infrastructure. Research is kind of\cb1 \
\
\cb3 Jenitta Gnana 0 minutes 26 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 operate in their own terms, in their own systems. A lot of the time the data is sitting on people's devices. And yeah, so it's like a lot of complexity that we're dealing with with researchers. What we're trying to solve for is kind of reducing the complexity, building in the governance model for researchers.\cb1 \
\
\cb3 Jenitta Gnana 0 minutes 47 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 and also helping them better comply to kind of the policies and laws which they need to adhere to as part of the research and development. Typically, research is a huge kind of revenue mechanism for universities. So a lot of universities apply for grants and\cb1 \
\
\cb3 Jenitta Gnana 1 minute 6 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 The way to do that is to hopefully have a strong R&D team behind you, and hopefully Databricks can help accelerate your team's insights to, yeah, discovery of new, you know, new innovations or new insights in R&D.\cb1 \
\
\cb3 Jenitta Gnana 1 minute 25 seconds\cb1 \
\cb3 So, I know, Spandana, probably you probably know a bit about the complexities in R&D, but a lot of the times, yeah, the data is coming from different source systems. It's this different security models, different governance models, there's lots of complexities to get the data, so there isn't a single source of truth when it comes to the data.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \cb6 \strokec5 SR\
